    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0273" n="232" xml:id="pg232"/>

                <head>71. Information Memorandum From the Chairman of the Policy Planning Council
                        (Bosworth) to Secretary of State
                        Shultz<anchor n="1" xml:id="d71-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1983-07-13">July 13, 1983</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>View from Moscow—Red Team Redux</item>
                </list>
                <p>This memorandum updates the December 13 paper on the same subject.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d71-f2"/> It was drafted by the same “Red Team,” chaired by
                        Jeremy Azrael and composed of
                    specialists from S/P, P, EUR, and INR.</p>


                <xi:include href="d71-a1.xml" xpointer="d71-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d71-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d71-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, S/P,
                    Memoranda/Correspondence from the Director of the Policy Planning Staff, Lot
                    89D149, S/P Chrons PW 7/1–15/83. Secret; Nodis. Forwarded through Eagleburger. Hill’s initials are stamped on the memorandum, indicating he saw
                    it.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d71-f2" n="2" xml:id="d71-f2-content">
                <p>A copy of the December 13, 1982, paper is attached but not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
